The issue stems from how `this` is handled inside a regular `function`. When a regular function is invoked by `setInterval`, `this` does not reference the `Timer` object. Instead, `this` refers to the global object (or is `undefined` if strict mode is enabled).

Consequently, `this.seconds` does not access the `seconds` property of your `Timer` instance. Since `this` is `undefined`, `this.seconds` is also `undefined`, and adding 1 to `undefined` results in `NaN`.

